I wrote both briefs for issue #104, and the harness accepted them, so they're now fixed. I made no code changes.

**Builder brief:**
- Change `packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js` to:
  - take any number of files and check them in order;
  - read stdin when a file is named `-`;
  - treat a second `-` as a usage error (exit 2);
  - report an unreadable file on stderr and keep checking the rest.
- Exit codes: 2 if no file is named or any file couldn't be read, otherwise 1 if any row is bad, otherwise 0. I chose to have 2 win over 1 when both happen; the issue doesn't say which wins.
- Leave `packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js` untouched.
- Add `node:test` tests in `packages/jsonl-lint/test/cli.test.js` for each case the issue lists, and update the package README.
- Open one PR whose body says "Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/104", and make sure `npm test` and the `test` workflow pass at its head.

**Verifier brief:** one check per expect line, in the issue's order (six in all). Each check runs the program on small sample files or reads the stated thing at the PR head (the diff for `src/index.js`, the tests and README, the PR body and CI status). Each check's PASS and FAIL conditions test only what its expect line says. The stricter points sit under an Advisory heading that doesn't affect pass or fail:
- whether 2 wins over 1 when both apply;
- whether `- -` fails before reading anything;
- whether running with no arguments prints a usage message;
- whether the tests assert exact exit codes and output.
